Use io, alloc, core, and list.

A record ListNode has a value as a whole number and a next as a pointer to ListNode.

Define function make_node taking value as a whole number returning a pointer to ListNode:
    Let size be 16 as an unsigned number.
    Let raw be allocate size bytes.
    Let node be raw as a pointer to ListNode.
    Set node's value to value.
    Set node's next to no address as a pointer to ListNode.
    Give back node.
Done.

Define function build_list taking digits as a pointer to List of whole number, n as an unsigned number returning a pointer to ListNode:
    Let head be no address as a pointer to ListNode.
    Let tail be head.
    For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to n - 1:
        Let node be make_node(list_get(digits, i)).
        If head as an unsigned number is 0:
            Set head to node.
            Set tail to node.
        Otherwise:
            Set tail's next to node.
            Set tail to node.
    Give back head.
Done.

Define function merge_two taking first as a pointer to ListNode, second as a pointer to ListNode returning a pointer to ListNode:
    Let head be no address as a pointer to ListNode.
    Let tail be head.
    Let a be first.
    Let b be second.
    Repeat while a as an unsigned number isn't 0 or b as an unsigned number isn't 0:
        Let value start at 0.
        If a as an unsigned number is 0:
            Set value to b's value.
            Set b to b's next.
        Otherwise:
            If b as an unsigned number is 0:
                Set value to a's value.
                Set a to a's next.
            Otherwise:
                If a's value is at most b's value:
                    Set value to a's value.
                    Set a to a's next.
                Otherwise:
                    Set value to b's value.
                    Set b to b's next.
        Let node be make_node(value).
        If head as an unsigned number is 0:
            Set head to node.
            Set tail to node.
        Otherwise:
            Set tail's next to node.
            Set tail to node.
    Give back head.
Done.

Define function merge_from taking heads as a pointer to List of pointer to ListNode, index as an unsigned number, n as an unsigned number returning a pointer to ListNode:
    Let head be list_get(heads, index).
    If index + 1 equals n:
        Give back head.
    Let rest be merge_from(heads, index + 1, n).
    Give back merge_two(head, rest).
Done.

Define function print_list taking head as a pointer to ListNode:
    Let cursor be head.
    Repeat while cursor as an unsigned number isn't 0:
        Say cursor's value.
        Set cursor to cursor's next.
Done.

Define function release_list taking head as a pointer to ListNode:
    Let cursor be head.
    Repeat while cursor as an unsigned number isn't 0:
        Let following be cursor's next.
        release memory at cursor as a pointer to byte.
        Set cursor to following.
Done.

Let first digits be a list of 1, 4, and 5.
Let second digits be a list of 1, 3, and 4.
Let third digits be a list of 2 and 6.
Let first count be count of first digits.
Let second count be count of second digits.
Let third count be count of third digits.
Let first head be build_list(address of first digits, first count).
Let second head be build_list(address of second digits, second count).
Let third head be build_list(address of third digits, third count).
Let heads be List of pointer to ListNode.
push first head to address of heads.
push second head to address of heads.
push third head to address of heads.
Let head_count be count of heads.
Let result be merge_from(address of heads, 0, head_count).
print_list(result).
release_list(result).
release_list(third head).
release_list(second head).
release_list(first head).
list_free(address of heads).
list_free(address of third digits).
list_free(address of second digits).
list_free(address of first digits).
Return 0.
